It is easy to ask a person to be more patient. It is harder to ask what keeps making patience necessary.

A queue, a form, a rule: each contains an idea about the person who will encounter it. Whether they have time. Whether they understand the language. Whether they can afford to make a mistake.

Compassion is not only a quality of the person at the counter. It can be a quality of the counter, too.

{% marginNote %}

An afterthought, 02 September 2026: attention is not purely an individual responsibility.

{% /marginNote %}

## Where care is placed

We tend to describe care as an exceptional act, something a good person does when a system fails. But perhaps care can be placed earlier, in the arrangement itself.

This does not remove the need for kindness. It gives kindness less repair work to do.
